        {
          "headline": "Google says Gemini, Gemini Notebook, Gemini in Classroom and Search will be off by default for K-12 student accounts",
          "sources": [
            { "name": "Google", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/education/ai-learning-era-updates-2026/" },
            { "name": "Google", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/education/guided-learning-uk-japan/" },
            { "name": "PPC Land", "url": "https://ppc.land/google-will-cut-search-for-k-12-students-in-schools-that-keep-ai-off/" }
          ],
          "bullets": [
            "In a post published on 3 November, Chris Phillips, Google's VP and general manager for education, writes that \"Access to these products will be entirely off for K-12 student accounts until school administrators explicitly turn them on\", listing Gemini, Gemini Notebook, Gemini in Classroom and Google Search. The post gives no date for the change, saying only that Google will share more specifics with schools \"in the coming months\".",
