        { "host": "A", "text": "One figure to flag. Stateline, citing the NBC exit poll, reports that 56% of voters said AI and data centres played a crucial or major factor in their vote for Congress. That number does not appear in the NBC write-up we read, and the donor totals rest on CNBC's own analysis of filings." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "transition",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "B", "text": "And yet the spending on the build-out itself keeps climbing." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "section": "Compute, chips & infrastructure",
      "headline": "AMD's Q3 revenue rises 45% to $13.4 billion as data-centre revenue nearly doubles to a record $8.5 billion",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "AMD reported yesterday. Third quarter revenue was $13.4 billion, up 45% year-over-year. Gross margin 54%, operating income $2.8 billion, and diluted earnings per share of $1.46." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "And the data centre line?" },
        { "host": "A", "text": "A record $8.5 billion, up 97% year-over-year. AMD attributes that to demand for its EPYC processors and the launch of the Instinct MI450 Series GPUs." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "What's it guiding to?" },
        { "host": "A", "text": "About $17 billion for the fourth quarter, plus or minus 3%, a midpoint AMD says represents year-over-year growth of approximately 66%. The release also says Anthropic, Meta, Microsoft, OpenAI and Oracle Cloud Infrastructure are running workloads on the first AMD Helios rackscale systems." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "These are company-reported figures, from AMD's own release. Shares rose 6.8% in Wednesday premarket trading, which made AMD the exception among the data centre names." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "section": "Compute, chips & infrastructure",
