      "lines": [
        { "host": "B", "text": "Nikkei Asia reported this morning that US tech giants' off-balance-sheet debt from AI-related obligations continues to balloon, almost doubling in six months to about $3.2 trillion." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "How does that compare to what those companies own?" },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Nikkei's subheadline says Google, Meta and others' commitments and obligations reach 80% of assets. The headline puts the rise at 90%." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "And here's where we have to be straight with you. The article is paywalled beyond its opening, so we read the headline, the subheadline and the lede. Nikkei's methodology, which companies are included, and the exact six-month window are not visible to us." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "There's also a companion Nikkei piece headlined that five US tech giants' hidden debts soar to $1.65 trillion, a narrower scope that Nikkei does not reconcile with the larger figure on this page." },
