        { "host": "A", "text": "And the cost of running it?" },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Roughly 70 to 95 times the GPU time ordinary serving needs for the same requests. Anthropic also lists hard limits. The proof covers an integer version of the weights under greedy decoding, not sampled output. Context is capped at 1,024 tokens. And Anthropic says the paper, the formal protocol and the running code are not guaranteed to match each other." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "These are company claims, and none of the performance figures has been independently reproduced. TechCrunch reports there are no plans to deploy it at Anthropic or any other lab. The researchers call it intermediate progress, not a finished research agenda." }
      ]
    },
