     "bullets": [
      "The Financial Times reported that Oracle has cancelled a chip-leasing contract with Tencent that the FT had earlier valued at \"an estimated US$7 billion (HK$54.6 billion)\". The deal was a five-year lease across multiple Oracle data centres in Southeast Asia and \"would have given Tencent access to about 100,000 advanced AI chips that were not available in China due to curbs from Washington and Beijing\".",
      "The FT, citing two people familiar with the matter, said US officials approached Oracle to raise concerns about the deal, and that Tencent also received visits from senior officials in Guangdong, where the group is based, asking it to support domestic Chinese chips. The FT's headline frames the cancellation as coming under pressure from the Trump administration.",
